---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Trust-direction rebuild (Landing Lab D3). FACELESS BY DECISION (2026-08-03):
// no founder names, no founder photo, anywhere public. Made by DJs for DJs.
// The first-person witness story stays because it carries no name.
// Endorsement quotes still pending permission (T1/T2 in audit).
---
<Base
  title="About Save My Gig - Built by DJs Who've Been There"
  description="Almost four decades inside electronic music. Save My Gig is the first DJ Booth Intelligence platform: rescue, prevention and booth knowledge, free, no account."
  path="/about"
>
  <main class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <div class="status-line">The_Story</div>
    {/* Antonio's evolved draft, 2026-08-03, merged with the page's DNA.
        Deviations from his draft, each deliberate:
        - "nights" became "gigs" and "the night doesn't care" became "the gig
          doesn't care": HIS OWN RULE from the same day (gigs happen at any
          hour), and "lose GIGS" lands harder under a brand called Save My
          Gig. Same for "save your gig" in Why free.
        - his em dashes became commas/colons: the source-dash check bans them.
        - the "not an app watching over your shoulder" guard STAYS: it is the
          recorded defence against "intelligence" reading as an AI claim.
        - the euro-15 line STAYS as the mission's second sentence: his new
          mission line is the principle, the old one is the punch. */}
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">WE'VE WATCHED GREAT DJs LOSE GIGS<br><span class="accent">THEY DIDN'T HAVE TO LOSE.</span></h1>


    <p>Almost four decades inside electronic music, from local booths to international festival management, have taught us one thing above all: the gig doesn't care about your preparation until the moment it tests it. And the test is almost always the same. A USB stick. A player that won't read it. A clock that won't stop.</p>

    <p>We've stood next to DJs at the biggest moments of their careers while their drive threw <span class="mono">E-8302</span> at them. The ones who survived weren't luckier, they knew the sequence. Reseat. Second slot. Second player. Format math. Survival mode. Calm, in order, no wasted seconds. The ones who didn't know it lost sets they had prepared for months.</p>

    <p>Save My Gig is that sequence, written down. All of it. The critical path for when you play in an hour, the proper repair for when you have three, the deep rebuild for the morning after, plus the prevention system that makes all of it unnecessary.</p>

    <p>It's free. It needs no account. And inside Emergency Mode, nothing is ever sold to you. That's not generosity, it's design: a DJ in panic deserves a clear path, not a sales pitch.</p>

    {/* THE CONCEPT (Antonio, 2026-08-03). This page is where the philosophy
        is explained, on his ruling: the homepage shows what the place does,
        About says what it IS. His definition, verbatim in the project docs:
        a DJ Booth Intelligence Platform whose purpose is to help DJs make
        better decisions before, during and after every performance, through
        knowledge, organization, preparation and prevention. The pillars are
        his list (knowledge base, checklists, gear guides, emergency
        procedures, best practices, compatibility, firmware intelligence,
        booth workflows, performance preparation, future tools), folded into
        prose because this page speaks in paragraphs, not bullets.
        "Not an app watching over your shoulder" guards the one real risk in
        the word "intelligence": a 2026 reader hearing an AI claim. The
        tagline means field intelligence, anchored to a physical booth. */}
    <div class="panel">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">DJ Booth <span class="accent">Intelligence</span></h2>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem">Most DJs discover Save My Gig because something went wrong. They stay because they realize preparation is part of the performance. Around the emergency flow grew the pre-gig checklist, the gear that earns its place, a dictionary of the terms the booth uses, per-model compatibility, firmware histories nobody else brings together in one place, and the working habits that make disasters a non-event. One system, one philosophy: better decisions before, during and after every performance.</p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">We call that philosophy DJ Booth Intelligence: preparation, organization, technical knowledge and real-world experience in one place, giving every DJ the kind of knowledge normally earned only after years behind the booth. Not an app watching over your shoulder: it's what the most prepared DJ in the room knows, written down, verified, and kept current. Save My Gig is its home.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- The independence pitch used to be a faint one-liner on the homepage.
         Antonio's call: the homepage shows what the place does, THIS page
         sells why it can be trusted, so the claim lives here at full size. -->
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">Independent. And staying that way.</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem">No manufacturer pays for placement here and no brand edits our advice. When Save My Gig recommends FAT32, duplicate USBs or a specific workflow, it's because real booths taught us those lessons, not because a marketing department did. Technical claims are checked against official documentation, and where we are giving judgement rather than quoting a manual, we say so. Where the official answer doesn't exist, we say exactly that instead of pretending there is one.</p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">What started as knowledge shared between experienced DJs has grown into a collaborative effort: DJs, technicians and industry professionals, checking this against the equipment and the situations they work in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">Why free?</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">Because the DJ community gave us our careers, and because trust is the only currency that matters in an emergency. If Save My Gig helps save your gig, there's a <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/savemygig" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="bmc" data-placement="about">coffee button</a>, after you're safe, never before. Some gear links may earn a small commission; they never influence a recommendation and never appear inside Emergency Mode.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- [ENDORSEMENTS: pending permission - Eduardo Philipp, Richard Zijlma, Akio Ide, Carl Heath. One real sentence each, with roles.] -->

    <div class="panel panel-go">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">Our mission</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">No DJ should ever lose a gig to something that could have been prevented. Least of all to a €15 piece of plastic.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel cta-exit" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">In trouble right now?</h3>
      <a href="/emergency" class="btn btn-quiet-danger" data-event="begin_checkout" data-placement="about"><span aria-hidden="true">🚨</span> Start Emergency Mode</a>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:2rem">Questions, corrections, war stories: <a href="mailto:info@savemygig.com">info@savemygig.com</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
